  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members) worked per RBC-QM-02.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (age 72) | Open gap | No qualifying screening on record. The frailty diagnosis that had excluded her (cond-00189) was marked entered in error this morning (Dr. Lin, comm-00301), so donepezil use alone does not exclude her. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0005), outreach message sent (comm-t0006). |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (age 52) | Excluded | Hospice care during 2026: St. Brigid episode eoc-00002, 06/16 to 08/21/2026, confirmed by the hospice discharge summary doc-00402. She revoked hospice for a clinical trial, but it still excludes her. No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (age 52) | Open gap | Her only FIT (obs-01732) was corrected to a collection date of 12/31/2025, which is outside the 2026 period. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), outreach message sent (comm-t0003). |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (age 51) | Open gap | Her 06/2024 stool DNA-FIT result (obs-01871) is now entered in error: the lab says the specimen belonged to another patient (doc-00401). Her 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 was never done, and an order doesn't count. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002), outreach message sent (comm-t0004). |\n\nFIT order windows run 10/23 to 12/31/2026. Each patient has a progress note recording the decision (doc-t0007 to doc-t0010). The four items that arrived during the work (inbox-a0001 to a0004) were reviewed and closed with links. They changed the status of three patients (pt-0009, pt-0022, pt-0024) before any outreach decision was finalized, so no corrections were needed. Follow-up for Dr. Okafor: pt-0024's colonoscopy order sr-00003 from 03/2025 is still active but was never performed. I did not work the other inbox items (unrelated, already there when I started).",
